[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868610057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2868610057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2868610057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q-4QJ","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T07:43:22Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T07:43:22Z","body":"Just a guess, but could RivaTuner be recording the number of windows rendered per second, rather than what you might consider \"frames per second\" traditionally? With two windows open, you are in a sense rendering double the number of \"frames per second\" if each window is a frame.\n\nIf you try Godot in single window mode this might help confirm. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868610057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868908031","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2868908031","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2868908031,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAA__","user":{"login":"Neuroburst","id":69093127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDkzMTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69093127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst","html_url":"https://github.com/Neuroburst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T14:27:34Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T14:28:59Z","body":"Interesting, in forward+, the fps does not appear to appear to increase a lot in the mrp nor the editor itself\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5202c73-5e6e-41a3-8cf7-75200c1bdb99)\n\nHowever, I notice a drastically higher GPU usage in the open windows in both Forward+ and Compatibility even in the editor.\n\nMultiple Windows:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bb7e5202-ab43-4ed0-baac-537e14e2c526\n\nNo windows besides the editor:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/691405c3-d3f8-44c9-a28e-9d95339cce54\n\nThe videos might not be clear but just having all those subwindows open in the background added around 11% GPU usage\n\nHaving multiple windows increasing GPU usage which is my real problem, but I thought the increased fps might have been clue as to what may be causing it. My theory is that the editor is redrawing all the windows even if only one is updated? That means it needs tons of gpu to redraw every window besides the one updated. That would explain the problems in the mrp, editor, and my main project.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868908031/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868935666","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2868935666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2868935666,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rAHvy","user":{"login":"Neuroburst","id":69093127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDkzMTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69093127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst","html_url":"https://github.com/Neuroburst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T14:34:51Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T14:36:14Z","body":"I found this github issue which might actually be caused by the same thing that is causing my problem\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/79290#\nHowever, I cant find any mentions of GPU which might suggest its something else, and they say that opening more windows does not make it slower, which is not the case in my issue.\n\nIs it expected to redraw every single open window even if only one is changed? My current project deals with around 15 open windows which eventually use 100% of my GPU even when interacting with only one of them.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868935666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870191016","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2870191016","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2870191016,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rE6Oo","user":{"login":"Neuroburst","id":69093127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDkzMTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69093127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst","html_url":"https://github.com/Neuroburst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T20:49:55Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T20:49:55Z","body":"I just tested it, the GPU usage is still high even with the windows minimized. Also the same issue occurs in godot 4.2.2 stable.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870191016/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870192104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2870192104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2870192104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rE6fo","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T20:52:28Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T20:52:28Z","body":"> Is it expected to redraw every single open window even if only one is changed? My current project deals with around 15 open windows which eventually use 100% of my GPU even when interacting with only one of them.\n\nOff the top of my head, yes. Godot, at its core, is a game engine which means it comes with the assumption that you want to update the window every frame. This makes it I'll suited for non game apps at times. \n\nWe have a bunch of workarounds on place to help reduce resource usage for in-game apps, but fundamentally it is still a game engine. \n\nThings get even trickier when using OpenGL (which the compatibility renderer does). OpenGL was designed for single-window applications. The assumption was that games would never need multiple windows, so the GPU context is attached directly to a window. Therefore, when using multiple windows in Godot you need to rotate the context and assign it to each window when rendering. Which comes with a significant amount of overhead. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870192104/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870192885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2870192885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2870192885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rE6r1","user":{"login":"Neuroburst","id":69093127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDkzMTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69093127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst","html_url":"https://github.com/Neuroburst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T20:54:27Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T20:55:42Z","body":"Oh. But the editor has a similar problem since it has multiple windows as well? Is there some workaround such as to force a window not to redraw unless it is focused so that the OpenGL does not attempt to render it? My program doesn't need multiple windows rendering at once anyways.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870192885/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870194289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2870194289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2870194289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rE7Bx","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T20:58:15Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T20:58:15Z","body":"> Oh. But the editor has a similar problem since it has multiple windows as well? Is there some workaround such as to force a window not to redraw unless it is focused?\n\nThe editor renders at most two or 3 windows at once so it isn't as much of a problem. \n\nGodot will skip a window if it is minimized or fully occluded. In general the update strategy is based on whether any content changes at all. So the editor avoids updating _any_ window if nothing changes. But I don't think we have that sort of update checking on a per-window granularity. \n\nTo be clear, I suspect it could be added, but it would probably take a lot of work. But could be worth putting in that work if you really need it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870194289/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870196178","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2870196178","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2870196178,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rE7fS","user":{"login":"Neuroburst","id":69093127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDkzMTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69093127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst","html_url":"https://github.com/Neuroburst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T21:02:20Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T21:07:28Z","body":"In my specific project, which is attempting to be a windows explorer replacement, I aim to have at most 15 windows open at once, which takes quite a toll on the GPU. The only workaround I can think of is to make each window a separate process which is capable of avoiding updating its own window individually, but that would create a lot of issues for my project. I tried using Forward+ but it is very unstable and crashes quite often with multiple windows. Compatibility seems to have much lower GPU usage as well.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2870196178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885282984","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2885282984","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2885282984,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6r-eyo","user":{"login":"Neuroburst","id":69093127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDkzMTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69093127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst","html_url":"https://github.com/Neuroburst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-15T23:41:14Z","updated_at":"2025-05-15T23:41:14Z","body":"I think I've found something; `RenderingServer.viewport_set_active`. It appears usiung this I can disable all the windows that are not focused to prevent them from rendering.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885282984/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885294099","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106227#issuecomment-2885294099","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106227","id":2885294099,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6r-hgT","user":{"login":"Neuroburst","id":69093127,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDkzMTI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69093127?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst","html_url":"https://github.com/Neuroburst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neuroburst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-15T23:50:41Z","updated_at":"2025-05-15T23:50:41Z","body":"Ok I've just tested it and it fixed my problem! Anyone with this issue can just use `RenderingServer.viewport_set_active(get_viewport_rid(), false)` to disable the rendering per window","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2885294099/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]